WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.610
This is the singularity... one day at a time.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.150
Here's the last 24 hours in AI. Sorry... SI.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.770
Years into minutes. A security puzzle stumped experts for decades.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.120
Claude cracked it in under half an hour.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.900
The answer? Just timestamps, no backdoor. And the prize money went to charity.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.340
Models: DeepSeek's new Flash model is faster and leaner,

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.120
and beats Claude Opus 5 on some agent tests.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.500
And the coding app Replit swapped Anthropic out.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.160
OpenAI is its default now, its CEO says.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.650
Claude also designed quantum circuits up to 17 times leaner.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.930
Quantum computers could come sooner.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.580
In China, Kimi's new credit card turns everyday spending into AI credits,

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:58.400
up to a cap.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.940
Money: chip stocks just fell eight days straight,

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.350
their longest losing streak since 2008.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.580
Nvidia's Jensen Huang: all of this is going to pass.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:12.540
It's going to be transformative.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.880
Anthropic is reportedly seeking $60 billion for chips,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.390
offering Blackstone more than 10%.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.370
And Elon Musk says the only way to fix America's debt is AI and robots.

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.400
Not by saving.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.220
The future: Anthropic's Jack Clark says science will speed up,

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.830
and America's economy could grow almost 50% by 2030.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:43.360
And in Hong Kong, student Claudia Chan built an AI companion for cancer patients,

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.700
between appointments.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.720
The catch: Yelp, Delta and big banks are shutting AI agents out.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.640
And Anthropic's junior tech hires fell from 27% to 9%.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.210
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.170
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.310
Machines: an AI lab is offering free plumbing repairs in three cities,

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.840
filmed to train robots.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:14.500
Laptops on Nvidia's new AI superchip went on sale this week, from about $2,600.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.440
In London, protesters want robotaxi trials stopped,

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.530
over safety, traffic and jobs.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.440
Years into minutes. And the real gift is time. Let's spend it well.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.040
Every day, the curve gets steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.510
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.530
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.910
This has been the singularity, one day at a time.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.870
Feel the SI.
